@namespace SpaceSails.Client.Pages
@implements IHandleEvent
@using System.Globalization
@using SpaceSails.Client.Rendering
@using SpaceSails.Contracts
@using SpaceSails.Core
@using SpaceSails.Core.Interior
@*
    #251 item 1 · THE FACE THEY KNEW BEFORE, ON ITS OWN FILE.

    Moved out of Map.razor by PURE MOTION — the block between the two fences below is the block that was in
    the page, character for character. Every page member it reads is a [Parameter] with the SAME NAME (the
    fields keep their underscore, the methods come across as delegates), which is what lets the markup move
    without a rewrite and lets the suite's source guards read it through MapMarkup exactly as before.

    The `@if` that opens it stays in Map.razor: the page keeps its paint order in one place, and a closed
    surface still renders nothing. IHandleEvent repeats the page's own override (Map.Sim.cs) — without it
    Blazor would put an automatic re-render back on every event in here, which the page turns off because
    the HUD's refresh belongs to OnTick's 200 ms throttle. The .razor.css beside this file carries no rules;
    it exists to give the component Map.razor.css's scope (#251 item 3 moves the rules).

    The `@{ }` around the fences is not decoration: the block used to sit inside `@if (…) { … }`,
    which is a Razor CODE block, and a code block is where its first statements are legal. The braces
    put the moved lines back in the context they were written in; they are outside the fences, so what
    the source guards read is still exactly the lines that were in the page.
*@
@{
@* ── MARKUP BEGINS · verbatim from Map.razor ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
        @* #997 wave 5 · THE ONE CARD OF THE FOURTEEN THAT KEEPS ITS OWN WAY OUT, with the reason, and it is
           a fact about the ✕ rather than a shortcut. `.convergence-x` is a FLOAT: its own rule says so —
           "the card is position: static, so this floats to the right of the flow it sits at the top of" —
           and a float lands beside the line box it is declared next to. It is the FIRST thing in the card
           for that reason. Bare draws the dismiss as the card's LAST direct child, which is the whole point
           of the frame and why the other twelve could take it, so shelling this one would float the ✕ down
           beside the card's last line instead of into its top-right corner. That is a control moving on the
           screen, which this migration does not do. And it is the only card here with TWO ways out (the ✕,
           and "Leave it there" once he has answered), which is a shape a Bare shell has no room for.
           It gets a shell when the corner ✕ stops depending on source order. *@
        <div class="convergence-backdrop" @onclick="() => Dismiss(CloseTheFaceScene)">
            <div class="convergence-card old-crew-card" @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
                @* #992 · A VISIBLE WAY OUT OF THE ANSWER PHASE (owner ruling 2026-08-24). Walking away
                   without answering has always been legal here — the backdrop closes the scene — but a
                   backdrop is an invisible control, and while the three answers are up they are the only
                   thing on the card that LOOKS clickable and not one of them ends it. Same verb as the
                   backdrop's, so there is still exactly one road out of this scene. *@
                <button type="button" class="convergence-x" aria-label="Close"
                        title="Say nothing and go — you can leave a face unanswered"
                        @onclick="() => Dismiss(CloseTheFaceScene)">✕</button>
                <div class="convergence-stamp">🪞 @faceWho.Name.ToUpperInvariant()</div>
                <div class="old-crew-history small text-secondary">@OldCrewHistoryLine(faceGiver)</div>
                <div class="convergence-head">“@OldCrewScene.Opening(faceWho.Id)”</div>
                @if (_faceSceneReply is null)
                {
                    <div class="old-crew-answers">
                        @foreach (OldCrewScene.Answer answer in Enum.GetValues<OldCrewScene.Answer>())
                        {
                            OldCrewScene.Answer a = answer;
                            <button type="button" class="btn btn-light old-crew-answer"
                                    title="@OldCrewScene.Said(a)"
                                    @onclick="() => AnswerTheFace(a)">
                                <span class="old-crew-answer-label">[@OldCrewScene.Button(a)]</span>
                                <span class="old-crew-answer-said">“@OldCrewScene.Said(a)”</span>
                            </button>
                        }
                    </div>
                }
                else
                {
                    <div class="old-crew-reply">“@_faceSceneReply”</div>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn-light convergence-close"
                            @onclick="() => Dismiss(CloseTheFaceScene)">Leave it there</button>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
@* ── MARKUP ENDS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
}

@code {
    /// <summary>the page's `string? _faceSceneReply`</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? _faceSceneReply { get; set; }
    /// <summary>the page's `void AnswerTheFace(OldCrewScene.Answer answer)`</summary>
    [Parameter] public Action<OldCrewScene.Answer> AnswerTheFace { get; set; } = default!;
    /// <summary>the page's `void CloseTheFaceScene()`</summary>
    [Parameter] public Action CloseTheFaceScene { get; set; } = default!;
    /// <summary>the page's `Task Dismiss(Action close)`</summary>
    [Parameter] public Func<Action, Task> Dismiss { get; set; } = default!;
    /// <summary>the page's `string OldCrewHistoryLine(string giver)`</summary>
    [Parameter] public Func<string, string> OldCrewHistoryLine { get; set; } = default!;
    /// <summary>the page's `void Say(bool atTheDoor, string line)`</summary>
    [Parameter] public Action<bool, string> Say { get; set; } = default!;
    /// <summary>bound by the @if that stays in the page</summary>
    [Parameter] public string faceGiver { get; set; } = default!;
    /// <summary>bound by the @if that stays in the page</summary>
    [Parameter] public OldCrew.Shipmate faceWho { get; set; } = default!;

    // The page's own event dispatch, repeated: no automatic re-render per event.
    Task IHandleEvent.HandleEventAsync(EventCallbackWorkItem callback, object? arg) => callback.InvokeAsync(arg);
}
